The MCP server now offers a broad set of tools for AI agents: reading and searching content, creating, editing and publishing pages, managing constructs, and administering users and groups. Every tool checks the same permissions as the corresponding REST API call. A failed tool call now also returns a structured @problem@ (type, status, whether a retry may help, and the CMS response code and messages), next to its error text, so that a client can tell for example a page locked by another user from a missing permission.
